Sval: the installer's welcome page says what Sval is

NSIS's stock welcome text asks the user to close every other application
before installing. Sval's welcome page describes the browser in its place.

diff --git a/browser/locales/en-US/installer/mui.properties b/browser/locales/en-US/installer/mui.properties
index a4ebb900f4..78b0b08b10 100644
--- a/browser/locales/en-US/installer/mui.properties
+++ b/browser/locales/en-US/installer/mui.properties
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 # from en-US contains a \n.
 
 MUI_TEXT_WELCOME_INFO_TITLE=Welcome to the $BrandFullNameDA Setup Wizard
-MUI_TEXT_WELCOME_INFO_TEXT=This wizard will guide you through the installation of $BrandFullNameDA.\n\nIt is recommended that you close all other applications before starting Setup. This will make it possible to update relevant system files without having to reboot your computer.\n\n$_CLICK
+MUI_TEXT_WELCOME_INFO_TEXT=$BrandFullNameDA is a web browser that lets you organize your tabs into Workspaces and encrypts and syncs them to your other devices through storage you choose - no account necessary.\n\n$BrandFullNameDA puts you back in control over what information websites can collect about you, and blocks common tracking and fingerprinting techniques.\n\n$_CLICK
 MUI_TEXT_COMPONENTS_TITLE=Choose Components
 MUI_TEXT_COMPONENTS_SUBTITLE=Choose which features of $BrandFullNameDA you want to install.
 MUI_INNERTEXT_COMPONENTS_DESCRIPTION_TITLE=Description
